  "source_note": "Familiar anonymous melody (not the older Mozart KV598 setting). Complete Ebersberger/Jurtenland LilyPond melody, corroborated by Wikibooks ABC, transposed D to C. One-quarter pickup and two-quarter final bar preserved. The Forschungsstelle für fränkische Volksmusik documents this familiar melody in songbooks since 1915; about 1945 describes its wider adoption, not first publication.",
  "difficulty": 1,
  "practice_notes_de": [
    "Der Auftakt besteht aus zwei Achteln; vorher zwei ruhige Schläge zählen.",
    "Immer drei Viertel pro vollem Takt zählen.",
    "Die längeren Noten ruhig halten und den Balgwechsel vorher vorbereiten."
  ],
  "harmony_note": "Functional chord stream transcribed from the linked LilyPond/ABC source. It is not yet a mechanically playable bass part: reduce or omit unsupported triads and direction conflicts for the 8-bass Corso.",
  "rights_status": "Public-domain traditional anonymous melody documented since 1915; new transcription.",
  "rights_note": "Forschungsstelle für fränkische Volksmusik documents the familiar melody in songbooks since 1915. Jurtenland explicitly declares melody/text public domain and freely copyable. Only underlying melody and simple harmonic functions are transcribed. The older Mozart setting on Kinder wollen singen is a different melody and was not used."
